{"title":"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> is drawn on a set of equally spaced <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">lines</a> as shown. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ratio\" title=\"Ratio\">ratio</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of shaded region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the area of shaded region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is 11/5. Find the ratio of shaded region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to the area of shaded region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8207b79435a4bd499da7598fb44424c8a8499238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f66de27fa4434501c4ef6a4590f17a41809dd7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10)); for(int i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { fill((2*i,0)--(2*i+1,0)--(2*i+1,6)--(2*i,6)--cycle, mediumgray); } pair A=(1/3,4), B=A+7.5*dir(-17), C=A+7*dir(10); draw(B--A--C); fill((7.3,0)--(7.8,0)--(7.8,6)--(7.3,6)--cycle, white); clip(B--A--C--cycle); for(int i=0; i&lt;9; i=i+1) { draw((i,1)--(i,6)); } label(&quot;$\\mathcal{A}$&quot;, A+0.2*dir(-17), S); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{B}$&quot;, A+2.3*dir(-17), S); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{C}$&quot;, A+4.4*dir(-17), S); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{D}$&quot;, A+6.5*dir(-17), S);[/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"418\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the apex of the angle is not on the parallel lines. Set up a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coordinate_proof&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Coordinate proof (page does not exist)\">coordinate proof</a>.\n</p><p>Let the set of parallel lines be <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=X-axis\" title=\"X-axis\">x-axis</a>, such that they cross it at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f45893bed9f55213c5dcd4360f0777e75664e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 2 \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />. The base of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. The bigger base of region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36eee9eaded3a8c323d85046041a94a032ded392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{D}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> is on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d1e7375e601943b3bb958a24e41da8920d601a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. \nLet the top side of the angle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/42020f4e0a1e5094c0826912a37eec4216103f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x - s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"11\" /> and the bottom side be x-axis, as dividing the angle doesn't change the problem.\n</p><p>Since the area of the triangle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/d/ddd1952ffb713991003b4c82e0150177396b8271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"31\" height=\"37\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/4/9c4b4fd73c01793ee229b4148f3eb5c1fbcbbb2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\textrm{Region\\ }\\mathcal{C}}{\\textrm{Region\\ }\\mathcal{B}} = \\frac{11}{5} = \\frac{\\frac 12(5-s)^2 - \\frac 12(4-s)^2}{\\frac 12(3-s)^2 - \\frac12(2-s)^2}\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>Solve this to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f54cd3a10283b07a53df43000bb58675b939ff30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Using the same reasoning as above, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e94396ce2c04120e18cb8d82dcb475442d8e2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\textrm{Region\\ }\\mathcal{D}}{\\textrm{Region\\ }\\mathcal{A}} = \\frac{\\frac 12(7-s)^2 - \\frac 12(6-s)^2}{\\frac 12(1-s)^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"270\" height=\"49\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74c2e26e57a3cbfd6c52596c1d3e813a24e4492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{408}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the sections between the two transversals can be divided into one small triangle and a number of trapezoids. Let one side length (not on a parallel line) of the small triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and the area of it be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. Also, let all sections of the line on the same side as the side with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> on a trapezoid be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Move on to the second-smallest triangle, formed by attaching this triangle with the next trapezoid. Parallel lines give us similar triangles, so we know the proportion of this triangle to the previous triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c90fbc3c2fdddf66649c93c9dcafa35ef38c03cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\left(\\frac{x+1}{x}\\right)}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"81\" height=\"48\" />. Multiplying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c82cf76c497ec62c04f433242f343a4645d2b0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> as the area of the triangle, so the area of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8fc82e121c01034fef87ac28f73e7d4c0b465c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />. Repeating this process, we get that the area of B is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37cd83675c3a50f2db23f55135d49b28928cfb6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, the area of C is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001ffad031ec0afbda518bbbb91db68b071451ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />, and the area of D is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e05f727eb9547ebbd29cd7f8149ee193602e1be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We can now use the given condition that the ratio of C and B is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a6fd88c163ca4f35dd1e2d1e30dac4c7cf7a004.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17bdd9397a6beed5045ced7155615a81738a9a7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{5} = \\frac{2x+7}{2x+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/7332bd3faf2ac2e782a70a6f3f93e6db67efabc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>So now we compute the ratio of D and A, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5f24b2a960001878423f358a6fc61f3cbe2abe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(2)(\\frac{1}{6}) + 11}{(\\frac{1}{6})^2} = \\boxed{408.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"162\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>Edit: fixed misplaced brackets\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Bash)\">Solution 3 (Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the distances from the apex to the parallel lines be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and the distance between the intersections be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c71d3cea07d47807c9ebe6a35f063e86ce04a398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> We know the area ratio means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04523b4db211434f34508bf357a4fd6470db0f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+4a)(y+4b)-(x+3a)(y+3b)}{(x+2a)(y+2b)-(x+a)(y+b)} =\\frac{5}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"327\" height=\"43\" /> which simplifying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f6d79d9df230c9f0433e3c4e1220e7a4964ee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = 3ay+3bx.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" /> The ratio we seek is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbe703bed794f2be91eb796298bc0a6b948c9f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x+6a)(y+6b)-(x+5a)(y+5b)}{xy} =\\frac{ay+yx+11ab}{xy}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"437\" height=\"44\" /> We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f16cc6b89241608bea9879017ca622a4ef95541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = 3ay+3bx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" /> so the ratio we seed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9ab9868d22016177224cc6d7f2adb295c60812a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{33(ay+yx)}{11xy}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"101\" height=\"42\" /> Finally note that by similar triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db256f988581bf0b4df4417ab9f1b912fd4c8d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x+a} =\\frac{y}{y+b} \\implies bx = ya.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"228\" height=\"36\" /> Therefore the ratio we seek is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f09de8626d79a90e328a2bd9ad1594bc7a6a25e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{66(ay)}{11xy} =\\frac{66a}{11x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"116\" height=\"42\" /> Finally note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/7/9c733b79acc138f36078476bf2a9e2db681a1ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=3ay+3bx \\implies ab = 6bx \\implies a = 6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"340\" height=\"16\" /> so the final ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9eab706d251c7b23c273b1715679ae96e9bd8859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 68 = \\boxed{408}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9534073152223ee3dda2dd557b767432dc5f60.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10));  pair A = (0.5, 1.5); pair B = (8.5, 1.5);        // Horizontal base ray pair C = A + 8*dir(30);     // Angled ray  // Path forming the interior of the angle path anglePath = A--B--(C.x, C.y)--C--cycle;  // Create a separate picture for the shaded region picture shadedRegion;  // Fill alternating vertical stripes on the separate picture for(int i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) {     fill(shadedRegion, (2*i,0)--(2*i+1,0)--(2*i+1,6)--(2*i,6)--cycle, mediumgray); }  // Clip the shaded stripes so they only exist INSIDE the angle clip(shadedRegion, anglePath);  // Add the clipped shaded region to the main canvas add(shadedRegion);  // Draw the vertical parallel lines for(int i=0; i&lt;9; i=i+1) {     draw((i,0)--(i,6)); }  // Draw the angle legs draw(B--A--C);  // Labels along the horizontal base ray label(&quot;$\\mathcal{A}$&quot;, A, S); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{B}$&quot;, A + (2,0), S); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{C}$&quot;, A + (4,0), S); label(&quot;$\\mathcal{D}$&quot;, A + (6,0), S);  [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"472\" />\n</p><p>A parallel line perpendicular to the diameter of a circle partitions a triangle into two similar portions given it does not lie on one of the sides of the triangle.. A triangle's ratio does not change when the triangle is rotated about its circumcircle. Hence, rotate the base of the angle about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> until it is perfectly perpendicular to the lines. Like as solution 1, the base of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36eee9eaded3a8c323d85046041a94a032ded392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{D}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7f6230166a491e7a471a03829c792496576480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7bf42db84e4d2dbb7bf55476c12bf9f6233bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, etc.\n</p><p>We continue with solution 1 from here, to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/4/a74c2e26e57a3cbfd6c52596c1d3e813a24e4492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{408}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I\" title=\"2006 AIME I\">2006 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2006\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\